Source: Samsung S5E9945 vendor kernel (android14-6.1, 6.1.138 source tree),
net/netfilter/xt_addrtype.c, copied without modification.

The device kernel (SM-S921N, 6.1.162-android14-11) is built with
CONFIG_NETFILTER_XTABLES=y but without CONFIG_NETFILTER_XT_MATCH_ADDRTYPE,
which Docker's and Podman's iptables bridge networking needs
(-m addrtype --dst-type LOCAL). This builds the match as xt_addrtype.ko.

Build: scripts/build-samsung.py 6.1 --module xt_addrtype ...

Device (SM-S921N, 6.1.162-android14-11): loaded with `ksud insmod` without a
reboot; in a Droidspaces container, iptables-legacy accepts and lists
`-m addrtype --dst-type LOCAL` in the nat table.

nftables (droidspaces_netfilter.ko, TARGET=netfilter61)
-------------------------------------------------------
Source: the same vendor tree; upstream/ is generated by
scripts/gen-netfilter61.py <vendor tree> and upstream/SOURCES.json holds
the SHA-256 of each unmodified input. The adaptations are the ones the
android16-6.12 module (src/netfilter) carries:
- per-net nftables state (net->nft.gencursor) kept in net_generic storage
  (compat/net/netfilter/ds-state.h); CONFIG_NF_TABLES stays undefined so
  the native struct net layout is used;
- compat/net/netfilter/nf_tables.h is the vendor header with its
  IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_NF_TABLES) block enabled;
- each former module's module_init/module_exit becomes
  ds_nf_init_<unit>/ds_nf_exit_<unit>, registered in units.h order by
  main.c with reverse-order rollback and teardown;
- nat-inet.c supplies the INET NAT registration the kernel omits, using
  the native IPv4/IPv6 NAT hook functions (LOCAL_IN for IPv6 is
  nf_nat_ipv6_fn on 6.1).
Families: IPv4, IPv6, INET. Units: core (sets hash/bitmap/rbtree/pipapo,
payload, meta, rt, exthdr, counter, ...), objref, ct, nat, chain_nat, masq,
fib (inet/ipv4/ipv6), compat (xtables), limit, reject (inet/ipv4/ipv6),
log, redir. No bridge/netdev/arp families, no br_netfilter. xt_addrtype is
the separate module above.

Imports outside the KMI export list, resolved from kallsyms by ksud insmod:
nf_nat_register_fn, nf_nat_unregister_fn, nf_nat_ipv4_{pre_routing,out,
local_fn,local_in}, nf_nat_ipv6_{in,out,local_fn,fn}.
Loading installs no rules or hooks. Refuses kernels other than
6.1.*-android14-*. Not yet validated on the device.
